.TITLE "echo"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Writes arguments to the standard output. It is primarily used to display __text strings__ or variables in shell scripts and terminal sessions.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**echo "text"**
Displays the specified string of text.
> __"text"__ the string to display

**echo -n "text"**
Displays text without appending a trailing newline character.
> __-n__ no newline flag

**echo $VARIABLE**
Displays the value of an environment variable.
> __$VARIABLE__ the variable name

.DIV "SUMMARY"
While __echo__ is simple and widely used, the __printf__ command is often recommended for more complex formatting tasks. Use the __-n__ flag when you need to construct a line of output across multiple command calls.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"

documentation: __https://ss64.com/osx/echo.html__
